CREATED:20260427T184508Z
DESCRIPTION:A collaborative Duke University and Duke Kunshan University wo
 rkshop.\n\nDuke Kunshan University's International Master of Environmenta
 l Policy (iMEP) faculty will host a one-day workshop featuring a dynamic 
 panel discussion on critical themes such as climate governance\, biodiver
 sity conservation\, and new energy innovation. In addition\, the workshop
  will feature two parallel sessions for academic paper presentations\, of
 fering scholars an opportunity to share their latest research and insight
 s. This event seeks to foster meaningful dialogue and meetings between sc
 holars from both Duke and DKU\, encouraging the exchange of ideas and int
 erdisciplinary perspectives. By bringing together leading experts and eme
 rging voices\, the workshop aims to address the most pressing climate and
  environmental challenges facing humanity today and to inspire innovative
  solutions for a sustainable future.\n\n<a href="https://nicholasinstitut
 e.duke.edu/events/duke-dku-workshop-climate-governance-transition-pathway
 s-uncertain-era">See the full agenda and participant list</a>.\n\nRegiste
 r: <a href="https://duke.is/may7climate">duke.is/may7climate</a>
DURATION:PT7H40M
DTSTAMP:20260428T200902Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T090000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T200902Z
